4. ROLE-BASED ACCESS CONTROL
==================================================

Implement proper server-side role-based access control.

SUPER ADMINISTRATOR:
- Full control over the application.
- Manage all users and roles.
- Create, edit, suspend, and deactivate accounts.
- Assign teachers, counselors, students, and managers.
- Configure global system settings.
- Enable or disable online classes.
- Manage academic terms, courses, and classes.
- View and manage schedules.
- Manage announcements and surveys.
- Access relevant audit logs.
- Configure counselor availability.
- Manage grade-related settings.

INSTITUTE MANAGER:
- Access only the features explicitly granted by the administrator.
- Manage approved students and teachers.
- Manage class schedules and academic information within assigned permissions.
- Publish announcements if authorized.
- View relevant reports.

TEACHER:
- View assigned classes and students.
- View their teaching schedule.
- Enter and update grades for students in their assigned classes.
- Add academic comments where permitted.
- Publish class-related announcements if authorized.
- Access online classes when enabled and authorized.

STUDENT:
- View and edit permitted profile fields.
- View personal academic information.
- View weekly schedules.
- View published grades and teacher feedback.
- Read announcements.
- Participate in surveys.
- Submit feedback.
- View available online classes when enabled.
- Contact the counselor during configured availability periods.

COUNSELOR:
- Manage personal availability, subject to institute policies.
- View authorized student inquiries.
- Communicate with students through the counseling system.
- Mark inquiries as pending, in progress, or resolved.
- Maintain confidential counseling notes with strict access restrictions.
- View only the student information necessary for the counselor's assigned responsibilities.

IMPORTANT SECURITY RULES:

- Enforce permissions on the server, not just in the frontend.
- A user must never gain access by manually changing a URL, request payload, or browser state.
- Students must never access other students' private grades or counseling records.
- Teachers must only manage grades for their assigned classes.
- Counselors must not access unrelated administrative information.
- Administrative permissions must be configurable and checked server-side.
- Protect all sensitive endpoints against unauthorized access.

