8. ONLINE CLASS MODULE WITH ADMINISTRATIVE CONTROL
==================================================

Online classes are a required feature, but the administrator must be able to enable or disable the entire module without deleting its data.

Implement a global configuration setting:

online_classes_enabled = true or false

When enabled:
- Authorized teachers can create or manage online class sessions.
- Students can view available online sessions.
- Each session includes a title, description, scheduled date, start time, end time, teacher, and access instructions.
- Students can access the session only if they are enrolled or otherwise authorized.
- Show upcoming and completed sessions.
- Display appropriate status messages.

When disabled:
- Hide or disable online class entry points in the student interface.
- Prevent unauthorized creation or joining of sessions.
- Display a configurable message explaining that online classes are currently unavailable.
- Preserve all existing class records and settings.
- Do not delete schedules, grades, users, or other data.
- Permit authorized administrators to manage the module settings.

Important:
Do not pretend that a working video conferencing system exists if it has not been implemented.

Design the module so it can integrate with an actual video conferencing provider, such as Jitsi, or another suitable service.

If video conferencing integration requires additional credentials or configuration, provide a clearly documented configuration interface and a functional fallback state.

Never expose private meeting credentials or administrative secrets to unauthorized users.

